Grant anonymous (unauthenticated) access to a bucket or to a prefix with a
preset, implemented as statements of the bucket policy:

  private   no anonymous access
  download  list and read
  upload    write (and abort multipart uploads)
  public    download + upload + delete

The statements of other prefixes and the custom statements are kept.

Usage:
  nexoctl anonymous [flags]
  nexoctl anonymous [command]

Available Commands:
  get         Show the anonymous access of a bucket or prefix
  get-json    Print the bucket policy
  list        List the prefixes of a bucket with anonymous access
  set         Set the anonymous access of a bucket or prefix
  set-json    Replace the bucket policy with a JSON document

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for anonymous

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl anonymous [command] --help" for more information about a command.
